EAD'","norm_id":"nc9b20638f88a92f8","priority":0.6611,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Investigator focuses per-section stopwatch on du expecting an unbounded blocker, but the du returns non-zero via timeout at ~120s; the remaining ~1.4min stall is elsewhere (e.g. docker system df at line 540, also timeout-wrapped, or the curl health probes)"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the intended remediation mechanism (metric-position-independent publication vs. reordering) rather than deferring the choice to the executor, or give the decision rule for choosing.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.465,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"either sections are ordered so no metric can be starved, or each publishes independently of the others' progress. State which.\"","This is a real design choice (ordering vs. independent publication) with different reliability characteristics, left open."],"finding":"AC #4 offers two remediation mechanisms ('either sections are ordered so no metric can be starved, or each publishes independently') and defers the choice to the executor via 'State which', without the plan itself committing to one approach.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fdbcbec291d2def25","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria, bullet 4","norm_id":"nc99a70f49c295dd1","priority":0.335,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor picks reordering, which still truncates the last section under a worse stall; a reviewer expected independent publication."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Commit to 'each section publishes independently of the others' progress' as the durable fix (ordering alone still truncates the tail under a worse stall), and keep 'State which' only as a reporting requirement.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Consider adding a global probe-level wall-clock budget (sum of section timeouts kept strictly below TimeoutStartSec) and/or concurrent/independent section publishing, because per-section timeouts already exist yet still sum past 240s — reordering alone relocates rather than removes the starvation.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.465,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Code already bounds each section individually but has no aggregate cap (observability.sh:323/324/691/766) and the unit caps only total wall time via SIGTERM (install-observability.sh:41)","AC4 offers 'sections ordered so no metric can be starved, or each publishes independently' — but does not consider a global deadline that bounds total runtime deterministically below 240s","Plan explicitly rejects raising the timeout but does not engage the documented TimeoutStartSec=240<300 latch rationale (install-observability.sh:30-41, bug 1205)"],"finding":"A structurally-different and plausibly-superior fix — imposing a single global wall-clock budget across the whole probe (and/or running independent sections concurrently so slow I/O in one cannot starve later publishes) — is not offered or considered; the plan's ACs address only per-section timing and ordering.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fda77f2f63633e36a","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria (AC2, AC4) and 'That distinction matters for the fix'","norm_id":"na5c232f7d204cdb8","priority":0.335,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Under I/O contention several bounded sections each near their timeout; ordering alone cannot guarantee the tail publishes, but a global budget or concurrent publishing can","Reordering merely moves which metrics are starved rather than eliminating starvation"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add an AC requiring that the sum of section time bounds is provably below the systemd timeout, or that each section publishes independently (e.g. backgrounded) so no section's stall can prevent another'